{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe op-cert service does per-job boto3/SSM/region lookup and patches process-global key/principal/push state — coupling app config to one secret store, letting jobs observe different keys in one process, and creating concurrency/cleanup hazards. ADR 0098 retains SSM as a deployment storage option but moves application binding to startup.\n## Outcome\nAt startup accept exactly one of preferred `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` or compat `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`. Validate before queue/worker/network/workspace creation, copy into a process-owned 0700 dir/0600 file, build one immutable signer/runtime, and pass signer/principal/push policy context-locally to jobs. The process never rereads; restart observes replacement.\n## Plan\n1. Replace `opcert_service.ssm`/per-job key acquisition with startup composition in config/key-provider/app. Reject missing, both-set, unreadable, non-regular, malformed, encrypted/passphrase, or non-Ed25519 input before service work. The path source (`REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`) also needs a regular-file 0600-or-stricter check; the inline source (`REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`) has no on-disk mode. Both are copied to the process-owned 0700/0600 location, mode-checked after copy.\n2. Copy key bytes to a process-owned runtime dir/file at 0700/0600; never modify/delete the deployment source. Graceful shutdown removes only Rebar's copy; deployment tmpfs/restart owns crash cleanup.\n3. Replace global environment/state patching with a typed context-local signer, environment principal, and push policy passed through jobs/workspace/signing. Concurrent and timed-out workers cannot observe or mutate one another's context.\n4. **Thread the immutable signer through the out-of-`opcert_service/` producer seam.** The key/principal are read from `os.environ` in `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py` — `ensure_opcert_key` (`REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`, ~L169), `opcert_principal` (`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID`, ~L193), callers `mint_opcert_record`/`sign_opcert_manifest` — via intermediary `rebar.signing.sign_manifest` (`signing.py:529-567`, sole `mint_opcert_record` caller on the completion path), reached from the service through `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:sign_completion_verdict` (called by `opcert_service/jobs.py`). Convert these (incl. `sign_manifest`, which must accept+forward the binding) to take an explicit signer-key-handle + principal (optional `OpcertSigner` binding); the service passes its startup-bound context-local signer, so removing `keyprov.py`'s `os.environ` patching cannot silently break signing. The developer-local close-gate caller passes no binding, keeping the env/genesis default. Also route the push-policy site (`_push_mode`/`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH`) to the context-local policy when a binding is present, env default otherwise.\n5. Decouple the op-cert APPLICATION runtime from SSM/region: remove `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM` and the key-retrieval `AWS_REGION`/`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` from the opcert service env in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`, drop the app runtime boto3 need in `infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert`, and materialize ADR 0049's SSM value into the process file/value startup contract BEFORE the app starts, OUTSIDE the application (`infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh`). HOSTED KEY MATERIALIZATION (T10): the multiline Ed25519 PEM cannot live in a single-line `.env`, so mirror the `rebar-bot-signing-key` precedent (`fetch-secrets.sh:93-115`) — `fetch-secrets.sh` writes the SSM value to a 0600 FILE next to `.env` (ALWAYS created, empty when the slot is blank, per bug beb1, so the bind-mount source is never an auto-created directory) and exports only its PATH; the opcert compose service bind-mounts that file `:ro` at a fixed container target (like docker-compose.yml:234) and sets `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` to it. The file-path source is authoritative for the hosted deployment; inline `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY` is NOT used there. The shared `/rebar/prod/*` SSM grant `ssm_params_read` in `iam.tf` (co-used by origin-guard/gerrit, no opcert app-role) is NOT dropped — decoupling is only at the app-runtime boundary.\n6. Preserve ADR 0049's Ed25519/DSSE algorithm, trust roots/eras, producer, authoritative fetch, envelope persistence, guard, and no-workspace-push invariants.\n\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Startup component tests instrument queue, worker, network, and workspace factories and assert every invalid source fails before all four.\n- Filesystem tests assert source untouched, process directory 0700, copy 0600, stable bytes after source replacement, restart observes new bytes, graceful cleanup removes only copy, and stale tmpfs clears in container restart canary.\n- **Signer-seam tests** assert the seam (`sign_completion_verdict`/`sign_manifest`/`mint_opcert_record`/`ensure_opcert_key`/`opcert_principal`) signs from the passed context-local binding (not `os.environ`) when the service supplies one — proven by signing with a distinct injected key while `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`/`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` are unset — and with no binding still resolves via env/genesis (regression pin).\n- Concurrent/timed-out job tests use distinct principals/policies and prove context isolation, immutable startup signer, existing producer signatures, and no workspace push remote.\n- Structural tests assert `src/rebar/opcert_service` has no boto3/SSM/region import or runtime parameter after cutover; deployment assertions assert the opcert compose env carries no `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM`/key-retrieval region, the image needs no runtime boto3, `fetch-secrets.sh` materializes the opcert key to a 0600 file next to `.env` (always created), and the opcert service bind-mounts it `:ro` with `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` set to that target (shared iam.tf SSM grant untouched).\n- [operator-attested] Hosted op-cert/review-bot signing canary records deployment/run ids, source kind (never value), signature verification, restart result, modes, and redacted failure outcome.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nExpand deployment input first while the legacy per-job facade exists; pre-removal rollback selects the legacy facade, post-removal rollback needs the same startup source contract (signatures/envelopes stay compatible). The signer-seam parameter is additive/optional.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly-one source validation rejects every named invalid case before queue, worker, network, or workspace construction.\n- [ ] The process-owned copy is 0700/0600, stable for process lifetime, observes replacement only after restart, and cleanup never alters the deployment source.\n- [ ] Concurrent and timed-out jobs prove context-local signer/principal/push isolation, one immutable startup signer, existing signature verification, and no workspace push remote.\n- [ ] The out-of-`opcert_service/` signing seam (`_opcert_signing.py`, `signing.py:sign_manifest`, `transition_close.py:sign_completion_verdict`) signs from the injected context-local binding when the service supplies one, and the developer-local close path retains its prior env/genesis resolution unchanged (regression pinned).\n- [ ] The op-cert application runtime (the `src/rebar/opcert_service` process/container) has no SSM/boto3/region/key-parameter dependency: the compose service carries no `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM`/key-retrieval region and the image needs no runtime boto3; the key is materialized before start by `fetch-secrets.sh` to a 0600 file next to `.env` and bind-mounted `:ro` into the opcert service with `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` pointing at that target. The shared `/rebar/prod/*` instance-role SSM grant in `iam.tf` is deliberately UNCHANGED (co-used by origin-guard/gerrit secrets, not an app-role).\n- [ ] Secret/key sentinels are absent from repr, serialization, argv, logs, exceptions, output, fingerprints, provenance, children, and persisted envelopes beyond the existing public signature.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Hosted signing/restart/tmpfs canaries pass with the required redacted evidence recorded."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787028381306388001,"uuid":"f0cfa7e5-a583-4e19-86fc-d54bddbcdf25"}